I'm running RH7.1 on a UP2000, using XFree 4.1.0-25, using an
Oxygen VX1 graphics card.  I'm seeing the following problems:

  - Every few hours or so, the colors will rotate.  My nominal
    desktop arrangement has some red, some green, and some blue
    windows.  They all shift colors one step around the wheel.

  - Likewise, every few hours or so, the monitor (Sony multiscan)
    will say the scan rates go out of range.

  - Much less frequently, from two days to a few weeks, the X
    server will appear to freeze, sometimes displaying something
    overwriting pixels starting at the top of the screen and
    slowly progressing downward.

With the first two problems, hitting Alt-Ctrl-F1 to get to a text
console, then hitting Alt-Ctrl-F7 to return to the X server seems
to solve the problem.

With the third problem, unless the user is very quick in hitting
Alt-Ctrl-Backspace to kill the X server (if that even works), the
machine eventually requires hardware reset.  It appears the X
server grows in size--I've seen around 1.5GB in process size.
The disks make sounds and blink the front-panel light as if the
machine was paging heavily (thrashing).  One time, the X server
was huge and was ignoring "kill" commands issued from a serial
terminal.  I sent a "kill -9" to the X server, and the shell
prompt on the serial terminal never came back.

Any suggestions?

Is it feasible to use the "limit" command to keep the X server
from growing too huge, such that it would hit the limit and die,
terminating the user session, putting the system back into a
useful state (after logging in again, of course)?

(In case it matters, RAM is 1.25GB, swap space is about 3GB (disk
is cheap), and graphics resolution is 1600x1200 at 24/32 bit
colot.)

Thanks.

Robert Riches
rm.riches@verizon.net




