Hello Ted,

Jay Estabrook, Jeff Wiedermeier and myself are the only three people that I
know of that work on Alpha Linux everyday. In our Lab we do have one
of almost every Alpha System ever made for testing.  None of us has been
able to spend as much time as we would like on the kernel.org kernel, as
we have other duties to perform.  I hope to have more time in the future.

It is not really a question of anybody taking over for Linus.  It is more of a
question of whether or not Linus wants anybody to take over.

I do have some students at UNH that build the gnu toolchain for Alpha everyday
from CVS.  This has helped keep the toolchain for Alpha up to date.  Next week,
I will have them add the kernel.org kernel to the autobuild system for both 2.4.x
and 2.5.x.  This should catch some of the more obvious regressions like compilation
failures.

I hope this helps.

Best Regards,


--George


