Sure did.  I compiled all the prerequisites (there are plenty) from the 
rawhide source rpms with no problems.  Qt 3.0.5 is the one I used from 
rawhide.  I found it easiest to compile all the requirements from SRPM 
because it helped me track down everything I needed.  However, the actual KDE 
I used the fresh tarballs from kde.org.

Works great, next time around I'll try it using -mcpu=ev56 optimizations.  If 
anyone wants to report back on those results I would love to hear it.

For those who haven't used KDE3, it is a big improvement over 2.2.  (Not 
intended to start a gnome/kde war, just reporting on the differences in 
versions.)

Ted

