On Fri, Nov 08, 2002 at 07:38:45AM +0000, Thorsten Kranzkowski wrote:
> 
> I will give my patch another thought and I will feed it to you in smaller 
> pieces and with comments.

You will have much better chances for correctness and acceptance if
you will try to _reduce_ number of casts by making sure that types of
objects agree, if only possible, instead of sprinkling code with extra
casts.  Every such thing is a potential spot for a masked bug although
side effects of a missed signed/unsigned comparison can also be nasty.
But if you want a unsigned constant with all bits on then ~0UL is surely
preferable over casting (-1) to unsigned long; even if just for clarity.

BTW - contrary to claim by Richard I found something like 45 lines
changed in that patch insted of "hundreds". :-)  No, I am not trying
to convince anybody that this number is small enough.

   Michal




