On Sat, Nov 09, 2002 at 01:07:17AM +0000, Thorsten Kranzkowski wrote:
> 
> diff -ur linux-2.5.46/arch/alpha/kernel/time.c linux-2.5.46-ds20/arch/alpha/kernel/time.c
....
> -		if (diff > one_percent) {
> +		if ((unsigned long)diff > one_percent) {
....

This reminds me and has really nothing to do with signs on casts. :-)

One percent is 36 secons per hour.  With such big drift I was always
getting "frequncy bogus" and a clock which was loosing big time all the
time (bad puns somewhat intended :-).  In kernels I am using currently I
have now dot_one_percent, i.e. I dropped that down by a factor of 100
and clocks started to behave.  I see in /proc/cpu:

cycle frequency [Hz]	: 796692134

instead of 800000000 as before and that is how it should be.

  Michal




