On a mailing list it is really better to put small patches
"in-line" instead of making them into attachments.  This assumes,
of course, that you are not using some broken mailer which plays
games with a white space.  Then change your mailer.

Peeking into ethernet packets indeed has often alignment requirements
which are different then those desired by Alpha.  Forcing alignments is
usually not the answer.  I do not remember when 'ping' used in Red Hat
distribution had problems for the last time.  It was fixed quite a while
ago.

> The extra stuff (the whitespace, and the 
> different conversion specifier) is probably just stylistic 
> changes--the patch was apparently produced by a Gentoo developer
> found by google, not by me. ;)

I would have to see the whole source context but I very strongly suspect
that changing to "%hd" specifier actually introduces an error.  This may
work for short turnaround times.  In any case it likely would be wise
not to reinvent (badly) a wheel.

  Michal




