I recently ran into some problems compiling Linux-PAM, and I've 
traced it back to a deficiency in the current GNU toolchain for 
alpha (gcc-3.2, glibc-2.2.5, binutils-2.13).  Apparently, a 
shared object is not permitted to reference its own global 
variables; whenever I try to compile a library that does this, 
ld complains about "gp-relative relocations" and refuses to 
link.

Is this normal on alpha platforms?  It's most certainly not 
normal on x86...

