On Tue, Nov 12, 2002 at 07:04:00PM -0500, Peter Petrakis wrote:
> //          ret= ASM("ldl_l   %v0,(%a0);", dest);
>             asm  ( "ldl_l %0,(%16)": "=r" (ret): "p"(dest) );
> 
>             temp= ASM("addl   %a0,1,%v0;\
>                   stl_c   %v0,(%a1) ;",ret,dest);

Incidentally, the original asm is broken as well, unless you're 
going to get guarantees from somewhere that DU won't move a 
memory access in between the ldl_l and stl_c.  You have to do
this as a single block of asm text.


