Where did you get Redhat 7.3 for the 64-bit Alpha (AXP)
architecture?  :-)  Redhat 7.2 is the most recently announced
version.  Are you sure you have the right mailing list?

As root, run 'linuxconf' (without the quotes).  There is a
section for creating/maintaining normal user accounts.  The
GUI lets you set a bunch of account parameters.  Once the
account is created, just log in as that user.  If said user
needs root privileges every so often, use 'su' and give the
root password.

