Hi,

to let you (esp. Jay, Michal) know that I am by no means ungrateful, a
little recp on this older subject.

I had tried to install rh72-axp on an AS200 (Avanti), but no matter
what ramdisk I used, the kernel never could see the root device
(/dev/scd, /dev/scd0/, etc.)

Jay and Michal gave a few suggestions, but none of those that where
MILO-related helped. I think I tried all possible permutations of
newer and older ldmilo.exe, linload.exe and milo-avanti, but to me it
seems that the ramdisks never got loaded.

I since switched to SRM - which I did not want to use in the first
place because all my other alphas are SRM-less Ruffians running fine
with MILO - and installed without any problems.

So thanks to all who helped, be it with hints on MILO and ramdisks or
on how to get the thing going with srm.

Ingo




