On Fri, Nov 15, 2002 at 04:24:44PM +0100, Helge Kreutzmann wrote:
> 
> we've got the 2.4.9 binary kernel from RedHat running
> (kernel-smp-2.4.9-40) SMP (we are still trying to compile it
> ourselves :-(() and there is one problem left:
> 
> The clock seems to be constantly wrong. ntpdate is now run every 10
> minutes and it shows a clock skew every update:

If the kernel you are using is GENERIC, then the problem is that
for RAWHIDE, HZ should be 1200 (that is 1200 ticks/sec), whereas
the GENERIC HZ is always 1024, regardless of the platform running it.

You MUST build a RAWHIDE-specific kernel to get the HZ set correctly
(see include/asm-alpha/param.h).

 --Jay++

