On Sat, Nov 16, 2002 at 12:22:43AM -0000, Damien Dye wrote:
> I have time problems on my LX164 machine too.
> I do use NTP to fix them but wonder why it does it!

I believe that tolerances on a clock calibration (that 'one_percent'
variable) are too big.  Before I tightened them up I was always getting
an estimated frequency on UP1500, instead of a hardware clock reading,
and a system clock was drifting by few seconds per hour - which is a
lot.

   Michal




