Nelson Brito wrote:
>>>Is there any way to recover a lost partition table?  I lost the
>>>partiton table on a ide disk and now i can't see anything on that
>>>disk, i can't even run fdisk on that thing...
>>
>>Try gpart.

this is an ugly problem to solve. You can start by findind a first partition.  like /boot by setting the whole disk to 
one partition. then when you know the size of /boot you can try setting a patition for /boot and using the rest of the 
disk as partition 2. then look at the type and get a size. You then can set the size for the next partition.

This will take a lot of time. Be willing to spend a full day or more with no guarentee of luck.



