On Mon, Nov 18, 2002 at 11:05:08PM -0000, Peter Watkinson wrote:
> 
> I'm trying to upgrade from rh7.1 to 7.2. I've downloaded CD1 and now the
> docs cd.
> 
> However when I boot after milo using
> 
> boot      hdc:/kernels/vmlinux.gz    root=/dev/hdc
> 
> with hdc being my ide cdrom
> 
> It starts to boot the kernel but then seems to say it can't find the driver
> for an ide cdrom.
> 
> Do you need a scsi cdrom?

No, you need a different boot command, since the distros are organized
in a different fashion:

	boot hdc:/kernels/vmlinux.gz initrd=/images/cdrom.img

Good luck.

