On Wednesday 20 November 2002 02:48 pm, Ted Goodridge wrote:
> Have you tried using the rawhide rpm?  That compiled fine for me.

It *compiles* fine, even without the patch. I think he's more concerned about 
getting it to actually *run*, which it doesn't, because XFree's ELF loader 
isn't quite complete in 4.2.[01]. 

You might want to check out gentoo's patches for XFree - I'm running XFree 
4.2.1 on a alpha/gentoo system (entirely compiled with gcc 3.2) with no 
problems. The patch tarball is here:

http://www.ibiblio.org/pub/Linux/distributions/gentoo/distfiles/XFree86-4.2.1-patches-1.1.tar.bz2

095_alpha_4.2.1-alpha-gcc3-gprel-fix.patch fixes the relocation problems, but 
there are many other useful patches in there - you might want to apply 
*_alpha_*.patch and *-pic.patch. The relocation patch I saw here months and 
months ago had a typo in it, which is fixed in the gentoo version.

-will




