On Tue, Nov 26, 2002 at 01:52:08PM -0600, Kelledin wrote:
> 
> Well, ok...the problem's not quite what I thought it was.  I'm 
> getting the following error message, though:
> 
> "Error: macro requires $at register while noat in effect"
> 
> This is what's causing it to punt.  Apparently, gcc is generating 
> slightly out-of-whack assembly language...

This actually sounds like you have broken binutils or your compiler
specs file is not up to snuff.  Digging through my archives seems to
indicate that I have seen that last time at the beginning of 1998.  The
following was the answer from Richard Henderson: "You'll have to arrange
for -m21164a to be passed to the assembler, perhaps via the specs file."

Check axp-list archives from that period and somewhat earlier and
you can possibly find more.

  Michal




